# {{.Project}}

Generated Pipecat voice agent, compiled by `unmute` from a declarative spec. Do
not edit by hand — change the source spec and recompile.

## Quickstart

```sh
cp .env.example .env                      # then fill in your keys
{{if .Telephony}}uv run uvicorn telephony:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 7860
{{else}}
uv run bot.py                             # web: open the URL it prints
uv run --extra console bot.py console     # terminal: talk over local mic/speaker
{{end}}
```
{{if .Telephony}}
This project uses the
`pipecat/carrier-websocket/{{.Telephony.Carrier}}` route and contains only that
carrier adapter.

The server exposes only the endpoints selected by the source channel:

{{if .Telephony.HasInbound}}- Signed carrier ingress at `/telephony/inbound`.
{{end}}{{if .Telephony.HasOutbound}}- Authenticated outbound start at
  `/telephony/outbound`.
{{end}}- One-use media URLs under `/telephony/ws/{token}`.
- Signed status callbacks at `/telephony/status`.

{{if .Telephony.HasInbound}}
{{if eq .Telephony.Carrier "twilio"}}Configure the Twilio phone-number voice
webhook to the inbound URL and its status callback to the status URL.
{{else if eq .Telephony.Carrier "telnyx"}}Configure a Telnyx Voice API
Application for API version 2, point its webhook URL at the inbound URL, and
assign the phone number to that application.
{{else if eq .Telephony.Carrier "plivo"}}Configure a Plivo Voice XML
Application with its POST Answer URL set to the inbound URL and its Hangup URL
set to the status URL, then assign the phone number to that application.
{{end}}
{{end}}The public origin must exactly match `UNMUTE_PUBLIC_URL` or signature
validation will reject the request.

Normal logs default to `INFO`. Setting `UNMUTE_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` also enables
upstream Pipecat parser diagnostics, which may include caller phone numbers;
use debug logging only in a controlled environment.

This route remains provisional until its credentialed smoke passes.
{{else}}
`uv` installs the pinned dependencies on first run. The Pipecat dev runner
serves a WebRTC test client you can open in the browser. Console mode needs the
`console` extra (pyaudio; `brew install portaudio` first on macOS).
{{if .DailyCarrier}}
Those two are for talking to the agent right now, with no phone involved. For a
real phone call through your own number, deploy first and then follow
